# Code owners
#
# A change under these paths alters what the project *promises*, not just how it
# works, so it should never merge without the owner having looked at it.
#
# This file adds an automatic review request and makes ownership visible in the
# PR. It does NOT by itself block a merge — that needs "Require review from Code
# Owners" in branch protection, which is deliberately left off: on a repository
# with a single owner, GitHub will not accept the author's own review, so
# turning it on would make every PR unmergeable by the only person able to
# merge it. Revisit when there is a second maintainer.

